{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_ERRORDESCRIPTION_SECTION_6_2_7_2_5_NVRAM_Manager","src":"manifest","doc":"ErrorDescription","page":51,"text":"6.2.7.2.5 NVRAM Manager\nDetection\nDepending on the stack configuration:\n Polling of the job result MEMIF_JOB_FAILED by the function\nMemIf_GetJobResult (see Memory Abstraction Interface above).\n Notification by EA with the callback function\nNvM_JobErrorNotification (see EEPROM Abstraction above).\nReaction\nIf write processing involved :\n[SWS_NvM_00213] [SWS_NvM_00296] Increment write retry counter.\nIf the number of retries is exceeded, the request is aborted.\nReport\n [SWS_NvM_00271] [SWS_NvM_00269] The error is reported to the\nDEM.\n The error can be reported by polling to the Memory Abstraction\nInterface with the function NvM_GetErrorStatus (job result set to\nNVM_REQ_NOT_OK).\nRecovery\nIf write processing involved :\n[SWS_NvM_00168] [SWS_NvM_00213] [SWS_NvM_00296] The\nNVRAM Manager controls the error recovery mechanism. The\nrecovery mechanism is (if configured) “write retry”.","caption":"6.2.7.2.5 NVRAM Manager","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_ERRORDESCRIPTION_SECTION_6_2_7_2_5_NVRAM_Manager","releases":["4.1.3"],"page":60,"hash":"46e53edb4320889b","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_ERRORDESCRIPTION_SECTION_6_2_7_2_5_NVRAM_Manager","releases":["4.2.2"],"page":60,"hash":"2d5497e80ea0d762","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_ERRORDESCRIPTION_SECTION_6_2_7_2_5_NVRAM_Manager","releases":["4.3.1"],"page":59,"hash":"bdedec1343d39091","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_ERRORDESCRIPTION_SECTION_6_2_7_2_5_NVRAM_Manager","releases":["R19-11"],"page":50,"hash":"ac2a6707a42b57f2","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_ERRORDESCRIPTION_SECTION_6_2_7_2_5_NVRAM_Manager","releases":["R20-11"],"page":59,"hash":"06897134b1be617d","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_ERRORDESCRIPTION_SECTION_6_2_7_2_5_NVRAM_Manager","releases":["R21-11"],"page":51,"hash":"ac2a6707a42b57f2","caption":""}],"releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","4.1.3","4.2.